n\nShe has an ordinary, everyday face: a slightly rounded jaw, modest cheekbones, small eyes, a broad nose and mild natural facial asymmetry. Faint under-eye shadows, visible pores and small skin blemishes give her an unretouched appearance. Her voluminous permed dark hair, thick eyeliner, blue-gray eyeshadow and vivid red lipstick make her styling conspicuous and flamboyant. Her makeup is slightly uneven and worn after a long evening. Preserve her individual features without turning her into a fashion model or a caricature.\n\nShe sits slightly sideways on the plastic chair, leaning against its curved backrest, with her right leg crossed over her left at the knee. Her left boot rests on the pavement, while her right boot hangs naturally above the ground. The black skirt lies across her lap, and her padded jacket bunches around her waist. One hand stays tucked into her jacket pocket; the other holds a lit cigarette halfway to her mouth.\n\nCapture the instant she realizes someone is photographing her. She abruptly turns her head and looks directly into the lens. Her eyes widen, her eyebrows rise unevenly and her lips part slightly, expressing surprise mixed with questioning suspicion. Her cigarette-holding hand pauses in midair. Her shoulders tense and her torso turns slightly toward the photographer, while her legs remain crossed. Her expression is immediate and unguarded, without a smile or theatrical exaggeration. A thin ribbon of cigarette smoke and visible winter breath hangs beside her face.\n\nExactly two adult passersby appear in the middle background, making three people in the photograph in total. On the left, a middle-aged woman in a faded olive padded coat and knitted hat walks past carrying a translucent plastic shopping bag with vegetables. She looks down, carefully stepping around an icy patch. A few steps behind her, a middle-aged man in a navy padded jacket and dark winter cap pushes an old black roadster bicycle, steering its front wheel around a mound of snow.\n\nThe two passersby continue their ordinary routines and do not look at the camera. Their postures are casual, with slightly hunched shoulders against the cold. Keep them smaller and more dimly lit than the seated woman, with a little movement softness around their feet and the bicycle wheel. Position them naturally along the pavement without obscuring the woman's face, cigarette hand, crossed legs or the salon sign.\n\nThe salon is a narrow, modest street-level shop with an aged aluminum-framed glass door, a concrete doorstep and a weathered rectangular fluorescent lightbox above the entrance. The sign reads exactly \"红浪漫\" in large red Chinese characters, with the smaller words \"美容美发\" underneath. Red adhesive lettering on the glass reads \"洗剪吹\" and \"烫发染发\". The lightbox has slightly uneven illumination and a yellowed surface.\n\nThrough the window, show two burgundy vinyl salon chairs, a long wall mirror, a narrow laminate counter with combs and spray bottles, folded towels, an old hooded hair dryer and a faded hairstyle poster. Cool fluorescent ceiling light mixes with a weak pink light near the glass. A pale curtain partly covers the rear of the cramped room. Scuffed surfaces, practical clutter and condensation along the lower window establish a small, everyday neighborhood salon.\n\nDirty snow is piled along the curb. Compacted footprints cross the doorway, and gritty slush borders the road. The cleared patch beneath the plastic chair is dark and damp. All four chair legs rest securely on the pavement. Exposed electrical cables cross the worn plaster facade, neighboring shop shutters are closed, and sparse amber streetlights recede into the darkness.\n\nPhotograph from a few meters away at standing eye level with a 35mm lens on a compact film camera. Use a horizontal composition, with the seated woman in the right third and the two passing figures in the left middle distance. Show her from head to boots, including the complete plastic chair and crossed-leg silhouette. Keep the full \"红浪漫\" sign visible above and beside her. Slightly hurried framing, a subtle tilt and a blurred sliver of a doorway at one edge create the feeling of a candid shot that has suddenly been noticed.\n\nHarsh direct on-camera flash mounted close to the lens, with no diffuser or bounce. The flash freezes the woman's surprised face and paused hand, illuminating her skin, down jacket, plastic chair and the nearest snow. It reveals natural pores, uneven makeup and small hard reflections on her lipstick and jacket fabric. A distinct shadow falls against the wall behind her. Her cigarette ember remains a tiny orange point, and the smoke becomes visible in the flash.\n\nRapid flash falloff leaves the two passersby and the distant street darker, with faint ambient motion blur. Weak pink and cool fluorescent salon light remain visible in the background. High-speed 35mm color-negative grain, slightly pale flash-lit skin, imperfect exposure and mild optical softness evoke an unpolished 1990s snapshot. Keep the main face and Chinese sign readable. No studio lighting, beauty retouching, glossy fashion treatment, exaggerated neon, modern cars, smartphones, LED screens, heavy sepia filters or added captions."], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 1, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "link": 74, "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "id": 4, "type": "CLIPTextEncode", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.41.0", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "CLIPTextEncode"}, "order": 11, "widgets_values_named": {"text": "A candid documentary street photograph set in a northern Chinese town in the mid-1990s, late on a freezing winter night. Outside a small neighborhood hair salon, an adult Chinese woman in her early thirties sits smoking on a faded red molded-plastic chair beside the entrance. She wears sheer black tights, 